  "body": "Slice 2 of #661: sections 4, 6, 7 and 8. Same pipeline, grid and style as slice 1 (PR #1116); nothing in `cargo xtask icons`' render/lint/check changed.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n- **31 new SVG masters** in `assets/ui/svg/` with their 32 px PNGs (`cargo xtask icons`; `--check` 0 breaches; the 41 `op-*` PNGs are byte-identical).\r\n- **Tool kinds -> icons:** `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_icons.rs` (exhaustive match on `ToolKind`, sibling of `op_icons.rs`).\r\n- **Status badges:** `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tree_badges.rs` - `status_badge` (what the row text already says: `BLOCKED` or warnings -> warning; else never / ok / stale; a stale path outranks its old warnings) and `row_glyph`, which paints the row glyph plus the badge on a disc of the row ground. `painted.rs` calls it (painted.rs shrinks 419 -> 414). `OpStatus` is unchanged, no new state, no command.\r\n- `IconSet::load` also leaves a shared copy of the handles in the egui context (`IconSet::from_ctx`), because the property pages are not handed an `IconSet`.\r\n- **11 PNGs deleted** (post, sim, fixture, debug-info, and the Tabler box-model, cube, transform, player-play, maximize, eye, eye-off). `assets/ui/LICENSES.md` is updated: 8 Tabler chrome glyphs remain, so the Tabler licence stays.\r\n- **`cargo xtask icons --sheet` labels each icon** with its file stem, using a 3x5 bitmap font of our own (`xtask/src/icon_font.rs`). **PROCESS_VERSION 25 -> 26** (xtask is a process file).\r\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/661-icons-tools-tree.md`.\r\n\r\n## Icons by section (all drawn original; none from Tabler; nothing from SolidCraft, HSMWorks, Fusion or any CAM product)\r\n- **4. Tool kinds (13):** end mill, ball nose, bull nose, drill, tap, boring bar, turning insert, grooving blade, threading insert, form gauge, chamfer mill (`ToolKind::Taper`, which the UI calls a chamfer mill), probe, and, **beyond the checklist, plasma torch** (`ToolKind::Torch`, #670).\r\n  - Mill tools hang from a solid holder block. Lathe tools run left from a solid tool-post block on the right (the turning ops have their chuck on the left).\r\n  - That frame is what keeps Drill the tool apart from Drill the op, and Probe the tool apart from Probe the op.\r\n- **6. Tree rows (7):** setup, part/model, stock, work offset, fixture, machine, operations folder.\r\n- **7. Badges (4):** not generated (ring), OK (disc with a check), stale (disc with clock hands), warning (triangle with \"!\"). They are solid shapes with the mark cut out (even-odd fill) so they read at 9 px.\r\n- **8. Actions (7):** generate (raster path, arrow and spark), post (page with an arrow out), simulate (play mark with speed lines), show, hide, frame all, debug info.\r\n\r\n## Wired / drawn but not wired\r\n- **Wired:**\r\n  - Tool library rows in the browser.\r\n  - The setup's Tool list table.\r\n  - A glyph of the selected tool's kind beside the op page's tool picker. The combo's items stay text: an icon per item needs a custom popup.\r\n  - The Setups, Machine and Operations tree rows. Machine wore the simulate glyph and Operations the generate glyph until now.\r\n  - The ribbon Setups door (now the setup glyph instead of the vise).\r\n  - Status badges on every op row.\r\n  - All 7 actions, through the existing `Icon` slots (same keys, new files).\r\n- **Not wired:** the Tools page Catalog rows and its summary line in `pages.rs` (1000+ lines; the 400-line law said do not grow it). Setup *node* rows keep their radio, not an icon. The warning badge has a real data source (`tool_problem_of` plus the cached warnings), so nothing is left drawn but unwired.\r\n\r\n## Least happy with\r\n- `tool-form` (could pass for goggles).\r\n- `act-generate`.\r\n- Redrawn after the first review round:\r\n  - `tree-part` is now a stepped solid and `tree-stock` a plain block, so they no longer read alike at 16 px.\r\n  - `tree-fixture` is now two tall jaws, the clamped part and the screw bar, no longer a dense block.\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n- **Pinning tests:**\r\n  - `every_tool_kind_has_its_own_svg_mastered_icon`: enumerates the kinds from the editor's own kind numbering, not a hand list; every kind gets a distinct `tool-*` glyph with a master, never an op's glyph.\r\n  - `tree_rows_badges_and_actions_are_svg_mastered`.\r\n  - `status_badge_follows_the_row_status`.\r\n  - Slice 1's `every_op_kind_has_its_own_svg_mastered_icon` and its \"no two slots share a PNG\" assert still pass.\r\n  - xtask's `committed_icon_pngs_match_their_svg_masters` and the new `sheet_labels_wrap_stems_and_keep_the_family`.\r\n- **Gates:**\r\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`: 577 passed.\r\n  - `cargo xtask icons --check`: 0 breaches.\r\n  - clippy `-D warnings` on xtask and camcraft-ui: clean.\r\n  - `cargo test -p xtask`: 49 passed, fully green after merging main. The `lathe_post_css` gate-map break was main's own and is fixed there by PR #1187.\r\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on the final head: green (ui suites ok, xtask ok).\r\n- Merged origin/main (37d93ae5 and later) with no conflicts; PROCESS_VERSION stays 26, since main reads 25.\r\n- I looked at the 16 px contact sheet on the dark and light bands and redrew simulate (the first draft read as a figure).\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n- Not seen in the running app (no GUI launch): the badge's placement and ground disc, the picker glyph, and the tree rows at real DPI.\r\n\r\n## Snapshots\r\n- No file under `crates/ui/tests/snapshots/` changed. The browser tree, ribbon (Setups door, action glyphs), status strip and op page goldens will differ at the next cut's refresh.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Tool kinds, the browser's setup rows, operation status badges and the CamCraft actions have their own original icons; the tree shows each operation's status as a badge (#661)\r\n\r\nEffort: high (no escalation). Process change: PROCESS_VERSION 26 (`xtask/` sheet labels).\r\n\r\nRefs #661\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
